# Coding of the 75 benchmark reference rows (Junda's RQ1 benchmark, repo snapshot 69f3c26).
# Statements are loaded from the repo JSON files; everything below is analyst coding.
#
# level:    M = metadata content (what records should carry)
#           G = profile specification/engineering (principles, alignment, reuse, obligations, docs)
#           S = systems and processes around the profile (governance, validation, UI, exchange, review)
# problem:  P1 Discover | P2 Access | P3 Understand & assess | P4 Identify, link & attribute
#           P5 Legal & regulatory context | P6 Manage metadata records | P7 Engineer & interoperate the profile
# resp:     A new class | B new property | C new code list | D expand existing term
#           E constrain existing term | F already in base | G no term-level response | H proposed / not addressed
# sub:      minted (profile namespace) | imported (other vocabulary)
# terms:    (term, class, kind) with kind in
#           minted, imported, newclass (existing base term on a class it was not on), constrained, asis,
#           cvnew (code list created by the profile), cvext (existing code list extended), proposed, gap
# deriv:    std (prior metadata standard/spec) | proj (project report/literature) | exp (expert/WG deliberation)
#           prac (practitioner/implementation experience) | law (legal/policy text) | tech (technical considerations)

